"description_full":"Monolithic Power Systems, Inc. provides semiconductor-based power electronics solutions in China, Taiwan, South Korea, Southeast Asia, Europe, the United States, Japan, and internationally. The company offers direct current (DC) to DC solutions to convert and control voltages within a range of electronic systems, such as cloud-based and on-premises CPU servers and workstations, AI systems, memory, storage solutions, notebooks, infotainment, power sources, home appliances, network infrastructure, and satellite communications. It also provides alternating current (AC) to DC; driver metal-oxide-semiconductor field-effect transistors; power management integrated circuits (ICs); and current limit switch and lighting control products. The company serves storage and computing, enterprise data, automotive, communications, consumer, and industrial end markets through third-party distributors and value-added resellers. Monolithic Power Systems, Inc. was incorporated in 1997 and is based in West Palm Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael R. Hsing | Founder, Chairman, President & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $7.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $620K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $148K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $51K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Monolithic Power Systems, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $55.7B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 43% against a 13% cost of capital \u2014 a 30-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 55% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $666M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.35\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 191% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.905233968084614},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $44.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 19% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"3,167 Monolithic Power Systems, Inc. $MPWR Shares Purchased by Stephens Investment Management Group LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/3167-monolithic-power-systems-inc-mpwr-shares-purchased-by-stephens-investment-management-group-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795176178.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ETFs Are Net Sellers of Monolithic Power (MPWR) on Friday","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/etfs-net-sellers-monolithic-power-110206640.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794913326.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Monolithic Power Systems retreats 12%, weighed down by tech selloff","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4675343-monolithic-power-systems-retreats-12-weighed-down-by-tech-selloff","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795209665.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Astera Labs, Aehr Test Sys